exports[`buildAccessibilityVisualEditPrompt matches the placement prompt snapshot for GRAB_BARS 1`] = `
"Edit this photo of a home to show the accessibility modification(s) below installed, in a photorealistic style that matches the room's existing materials, lighting and camera angle.

Add ONLY these items:

1. Grab Bars
   - Quantity: 1–2 bars in total.
   - Placement: Only on the wall directly beside the toilet, or on the wall inside the shower or above the tub rim.
   - Mounting: Mounted horizontally (or vertically at a shower entry), anchored to the wall with round flanges at both ends, 33–36 inches (84–91 cm) above the floor.
   - Size: 12–36 inches long, about 1.25–1.5 inches in diameter, brushed stainless steel or a finish matching the existing fixtures.
   - Never place bars on vanities, countertops, cabinets, mirrors, doors or windows.
   - Never place bars on open walls away from the toilet, shower or tub.
   - Never add more than 2 bars.

Strict rules:
- Add ONLY the items listed above. Do not add any other fixtures, furniture, decor or accessibility equipment.
- Keep every other surface, wall, floor, fixture and object exactly as it appears in the original photo.
- Keep the same framing, perspective and room layout.
- If an item has no realistic location visible in this photo, leave that part of the photo unchanged rather than inventing a location."
`;

exports[`buildAccessibilityVisualEditPrompt matches the placement prompt snapshot for HANDRAILS 1`] = `
"Edit this photo of a home to show the accessibility modification(s) below installed, in a photorealistic style that matches the room's existing materials, lighting and camera angle.

Add ONLY these items:

1. Handrails
   - Quantity: 1–2 rails — one per side of the existing stairs or steps.
   - Placement: Along existing stairs or entry steps only, following their slope.
   - Mounting: Continuous rail on wall brackets or posts, 34–38 inches (86–97 cm) above the stair nosing, extending about 12 inches past the top and bottom steps.
   - Size: Round grip about 1.25–2 inches in diameter, in wood or metal matching the surroundings.
   - Never place handrails on walls or areas without stairs or steps.
   - Never run handrails across doorways or onto furniture.
   - Never add more than one rail per side.

Strict rules:
- Add ONLY the items listed above. Do not add any other fixtures, furniture, decor or accessibility equipment.
- Keep every other surface, wall, floor, fixture and object exactly as it appears in the original photo.
- Keep the same framing, perspective and room layout.
- If an item has no realistic location visible in this photo, leave that part of the photo unchanged rather than inventing a location."
`;

